# Prettier does not know that `$$...$$` is math -- that is a Quarto/Pandoc
# extension, not CommonMark. Inside a display-math block it therefore reads
# `_{aero}` as emphasis and rewrites it to `*{aero}`, and escapes a lone `_`
# to `\_`. Both destroy the LaTeX: MathJax renders `F*{aero}` literally, and
# `\_` is an underscore character rather than a subscript. These pages are
# rendered to the site by the root _quarto.yml, so the damage is user-visible.
# This is not hypothetical -- it is how the equations in 02_aerodynamics,
# 03_neuromuscular_control, dimensional_inconsistency_dcr,
# flaccid_drift_contradiction and tip_mass_omission were broken, and it
# reverted the fix on every commit attempt until this entry was added.
